1
00:00:00,938 --> 00:00:03,068
(Gablehouser:)We're hoping to have him
do graduate work here.

2
00:00:03,232 --> 00:00:06,482
- Graduate work, very impressive.
- And he's only 15 years old.

3
00:00:06,652 --> 00:00:10,532
(Sheldon:)Not bad.
I myself started graduate school at 14.

4
00:00:10,698 --> 00:00:14,198
(Dennis:)Well, I lost a year while my family
was tunneling out of North Korea.

5
00:00:16,579 --> 00:00:19,369
(Leonard:)Advantage, Kim.

6
00:00:19,916 --> 00:00:21,996
(Gablehouser:)I thought maybe you
could show Dennis around.

7
00:00:22,168 --> 00:00:25,508
(Gablehouser:)Let him see why we're the best
physics research facility in the country.

8
00:00:25,671 --> 00:00:26,711
I know you're not.

9
00:00:26,881 --> 00:00:30,221
(Dennis:)You don't have an Open Science Grid
computer or a free electron laser.

10
00:00:30,384 --> 00:00:32,974
(Dennis:)The string theory research
being done is a dead end.

11
00:00:33,137 --> 00:00:36,847
(Sheldon:)Excuse me, that is my research,
and it is by no means a dead end.

12
00:00:37,016 --> 00:00:40,056
(Dennis:)Well, obviously, you don't see it yet,
but trust me, you will.

13
00:00:42,855 --> 00:00:44,435
Dennis, we've discussed this.

14
00:00:44,607 --> 00:00:46,987
(Gablehouser:)We're in the process
of updating our equipment.

15
00:00:47,151 --> 00:00:49,321
(Gablehouser:)We welcome your input
on our research goals.

16
00:00:49,487 --> 00:00:52,027
We agree to look the other way
if you use 20 percent...

17
00:00:52,198 --> 00:00:55,578
...of the money you attract to smuggle
your grandfather out of Pyongyang.

18
00:00:57,245 --> 00:00:59,375
(Gablehouser:)We want him here, boys.

19
00:00:59,539 --> 00:01:01,039
(Gablehouser:)- Make it happen.
- Yes, sir.

20
00:01:01,207 --> 00:01:03,037
(Sheldon:)You can count on us. We're on it.

21
00:01:03,209 --> 00:01:05,499
What the hell do you mean, "dead end"?

22
00:01:05,920 --> 00:01:08,880
(Dennis:)I mean, the whole landscape
of false vacuums in string theory...

23
00:01:09,048 --> 00:01:11,388
(Dennis:)...could be as large
as 10 to the 500th power.

24
00:01:11,551 --> 00:01:12,551
(Dennis:)In addition...

25
00:01:12,718 --> 00:01:14,098
(Dennis:)Ooh, look, chocolate milk.

26
00:01:17,098 --> 00:01:20,018
(Sheldon:)I sense a disturbance in the force.

27
00:01:20,184 --> 00:01:24,024
[IMITATING YODA]
A bad feeling I have about this. Mm.

